{%- doc -%}
  Announcement-bar block visibility, computed in one place. Outputs either the
  index (into the given blocks array) of the first block that will actually
  render (-1 when none will), or the count of blocks that will render.

  Two consumers, both replacing raw `section.blocks`-based checks that a
  dormant block would miscount:
  - `_announcement` / `_vacation-announcement` compare their own index against
    `output: 'index'` for the initial aria-hidden state (a dormant vacation
    slide or blank announcement at index 0 must not hide every slide until JS
    hydrates).
  - `header-announcements.liquid` gates the carousel chrome (script, autoplay,
    arrows, pause buttons) on `output: 'count'`, so one real announcement plus
    a dormant vacation block does not render dead controls.

  Visibility rules mirror each block's own render guard exactly; keep them in
  sync when either guard changes:
  - `_announcement`: visible when its stripped `text` setting is non-blank.
  - `_vacation-announcement`: visible when `settings.vacation_mode_enabled` and
    the stripped global `settings.vacation_announcement_text` is non-blank.
  Unknown block types are treated as visible, so a future block type fails
  toward "shown and counted" rather than a blank bar.

  @param {object} blocks - The announcement section's blocks (section.blocks)
  @param {string} [output] - 'index' (default) for the first visible block's
    index, or 'count' for the number of visible blocks

  @example
    {% capture first_visible_index %}
      {%- render 'announcement-visible-blocks', blocks: section.blocks -%}
    {% endcapture %}
    {% assign first_visible_index = first_visible_index | strip | plus: 0 %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign visible_count = 0
  assign first_visible_index = -1

  for candidate in blocks
    assign candidate_visible = false

    case candidate.type
      when '_announcement'
        assign candidate_text = candidate.settings.text | strip_newlines | strip_html | strip
        if candidate_text != ''
          assign candidate_visible = true
        endif
      when '_vacation-announcement'
        if settings.vacation_mode_enabled
          assign candidate_text = settings.vacation_announcement_text | strip_newlines | strip_html | strip
          if candidate_text != ''
            assign candidate_visible = true
          endif
        endif
      else
        assign candidate_visible = true
    endcase

    if candidate_visible
      assign visible_count = visible_count | plus: 1
      if first_visible_index == -1
        assign first_visible_index = forloop.index0
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  if output == 'count'
    echo visible_count
  else
    echo first_visible_index
  endif
-%}
